title: JVM: the Truffle regex engine, to feature-complete
branch: pr/03-truffle-regex-engine

# Sections N5a (log lines 160..176), N5b (177..190), N5c (191..205), 46 commits.
# Groups are contiguous runs in original order except where a `# moved:` comment says otherwise.

= JVM/Truffle: a regex engine driven from QAST::Regex through a descriptor
The nqp-truffle module: a backtracking regex VM (RxProgram/RxVmNode) under
Truffle, a Cursor, the check harness and bench. The backend flattens
QAST::Regex once at compile time into an int array plus a string pool
(RxDescriptor.nqp), and the engine decodes it back; rxtypes it cannot encode
answer null and keep the bytecode path.
# NET-ZERO: the AST-interpreter design (RxNodes/RxLink/RxState) and the
# parsed-text driving of the engine are introduced and replaced inside this
# group; the text parser survives only as the harness's input (RxParser).
- a697a12a4 JVM: a Truffle regex engine, and the ground it stands on
- 9b1deedb5 JVM/Truffle: make the regex engine correct, and measure what that cost
- 5c117c32f JVM/Truffle: find out why the engine does not compile
- c67864dc2 JVM/Truffle: compile the pattern to a program so it can be compiled
- 1c38bae97 JVM/Truffle: drive the engine from QAST::Regex, not from parsed text

= JVM/Truffle: whole-regex shape, NQP captures on a Cursor, char classes
The descriptor encodes the shape a whole regex has; the engine binds to a
real Cursor and captures the way NQP captures; opcodes for the common
character classes, and a scan that measures something.
- b31685ffe JVM/Truffle: encode the shape a whole regex actually has
- 565f20ac6 JVM/Truffle: bind the engine to a real Cursor, and stop encoding captures
- 5de3afa26 JVM/Truffle: capture the way NQP captures, and encode captures again
- f72f71d0a JVM/Truffle: opcodes for the common character classes, and a scan that measures something

= JVM/Truffle: reach the engine from compiled code, compile rules to it
GrammarEngine/TruffleGrammarEngine and the wire format; every generated
runner starts a JVM that can run a grammar; a rule compiles to a descriptor
instead of a matcher. NQP_JVM_TRUFFLE=require turns a missing engine into a
failure.
# Introduces the NQP_JVM_NO_TRUFFLE whole-engine toggle, removed later in
# this file (see the `# spans:` note on that group).
- 6ca347429 JVM/Truffle: let the engine be reached from compiled code
- 723c3eecf JVM/Truffle: start every JVM so that it can run a grammar
- 787b8f103 JVM/Truffle: compile a rule to a descriptor instead of a matcher

= JVM/Truffle: five more rxtypes, the engine in Kotlin, and parity
The engine is ported to Kotlin; five more rxtypes encode; parity with the
bytecode path on the sweep. docs/truffle-grammar-engine.md records what the
diff does not show and the measurement against what the engine replaces.
- de41d6291 JVM/Truffle: write down what the diff does not show
- 391d7883c JVM/Truffle: measure the engine against what it replaces
- e277ce41c JVM/Truffle: five more rxtypes, the engine in Kotlin, and parity

= JVM/Truffle: name what a qastnode bail is about; run rakudo's suite
Lexical access on this backend is depth-indexed and resolved at compile
time, which is what a qastnode fix has to satisfy; a qastnode bail names the
lowered local it is about. Rakudo's own suite runs under the engine.
- 09cbdfbbd JVM/Truffle: record what the qastnode attempt is actually constrained by
- 2b69b9757 JVM/Truffle: run rakudo's own suite under the engine, which had never been done
- 4423777a0 JVM/Truffle: name the lowered local a qastnode bail is about

# ---- N5b ----

= JVM: shape-keyed helper sites, corrupt-capture reports, pending dispatch
A helper dispatch site is keyed by argument shape, not just by method; a
corrupt capture is reported where it is read and which half is corrupt; the
outer pending dispatch is restored rather than cleared, in realize too.
- 6bbce5b7a JVM: key a helper dispatch site by argument shape, not just by method
- 830076873 JVM: report a corrupt capture where it is read, not where it hurts
- 08d6ef4e4 JVM: restore the outer pending dispatch, rather than clearing it
- 7d5439d12 JVM: restore the pending dispatch in realize too, and say which half is corrupt

