- a95e2bc79 JVM: an explicitly-managed string must come from the C allocator

= JVM: raku-invoke at runtime, exact smart coercions, lazy object lexicals
Runtime invocations go through raku-invoke and the syscall gaps are closed;
the smart coercions have the dispatcher programs' exact semantics; object
lexicals vivify lazily and dynamically-bound code is repointed.
- cbe306d58 JVM: run raku-invoke for runtime invocations, and close syscall gaps
- 9d56f9cef JVM: give the smart coercions the dispatcher programs' exact semantics
- b1c5f9384 JVM: vivify object lexicals lazily, and repoint dynamically-bound code

