- efd29f30a Truffle engine: match a CR LF pair as one atom

= Encode backtrackable rules, with unencodable subrule calls as callbacks
Every rule the descriptor can encode runs on the engine; the bytecode path
exists only for the rules that still bail (NQP_RX_SURVEY names them), and
the NQP_RX_* triage knobs are where bisection belongs. Backtrackable rules
that call no subrules encode; an unencodable subrule call is carried as a
callback piece, and rule code runs against the captures made so far.
%*RX resolution has env-gated diagnostics.
# spans: the whole-engine toggle NQP_JVM_NO_TRUFFLE removed here was introduced
# in this file's third group (the "reach the engine from compiled code" group).
# The removal cannot be moved back: it touches QAST/Compiler.nqp and
# runtime/GrammarEngine.kt, which the intervening "five more rxtypes",
# "resolved-reference ceiling" and "eval server" commits also touch. Both stay.
- f3d300474 Remove the whole-engine toggle
- 5d9096c4c Encode backtrackable rules that call no subrules
- 9a655a95f Carry unencodable subrule calls as callback pieces
- b9382278f Run rule code against the captures made so far
- a68a1b550 Env-gated diagnostics for %*RX resolution

